00:52:36,521 --> 00:52:42,521
Blade is a 1998 American superhero film  based on
the character from Marvel Comics.

11
00:57:52,173 --> 00:57:58,173
The first installment of the Blade franchise, it was directed
by Stephen Norrington and written by David S.

12
01:03:07,826 --> 01:03:13,826
Wesley Snipes stars as the titular character, with Stephen Dorff, Kris
Kristofferson and N'Bushe Wright in supporting roles.

13
01:08:23,478 --> 01:08:29,478
Blade is a Dhampir, a human with vampire strengths but not
their weaknesses, who fights against vampires.

14
01:13:39,130 --> 01:13:45,130
Blade was released in the United States on August 21, 1998, and was a
commercial success, grossing $70 million at the U.S.

15
01:18:54,782 --> 01:19:00,782
box office, and $131.2 million worldwide.

16
01:24:10,434 --> 01:24:16,434
Despite mixed reviews from film critics, the film
has since garnered a cult following.

17
01:29:26,086 --> 01:29:32,086
It is also hailed as one of Snipes's signature roles.

18
01:34:41,739 --> 01:34:47,739
Blade was noted as a dark superhero film for its time, as
well as being Marvel's first successful film.

19
01:39:57,391 --> 01:40:03,391
It was followed by two sequels, Blade II (2002) and Blade: Trinity
(2004), both written by Goyer, who also directed the latter.

20
